## Usage

### Basic
`v-model` binds the Markdown; pass `uploadImage`, `ai` and `v-model:comments` to turn on image uploads, AI rewriting and comments.
::::TuffDemoWrapper{demo="MarkdownEditorMarkdownEditorDemo" code-lang="vue"}
---
code: |
  <script setup lang="ts">
  import type { MarkdownEditorAi, MarkdownEditorComment, MarkdownEditorUploadImage } from '@talex-touch/tuffex/markdown-editor'
  import { ref } from 'vue'

  const content = ref('# Release notes\n\nThis release rewrites the search pipeline: ==cold start is 38% faster==.')
  const comments = ref<MarkdownEditorComment[]>([])

  // Put the image in your own storage and return its CDN address
  const uploadImage: MarkdownEditorUploadImage = async (file, { onProgress, signal }) => {
    const url = await uploadToCdn(file, { onProgress, signal })
    return { url, alt: file.name }
  }

  // Hand the selected text to a model and stream back the rewrite
  const ai: MarkdownEditorAi = request => streamRewrite(request)
  </script>

  <template>
    <TxMarkdownEditor
      v-model="content"
      v-model:comments="comments"
      :user="{ id: 'me', name: 'Me' }"
      :upload-image="uploadImage"
      :ai="ai"
    />
  </template>
---
::::

### Collaboration
`collaboration` connects real-time editing: the editor sends and receives change sets and carets, and your adapter merges concurrent edits.
::::TuffDemoWrapper{demo="MarkdownEditorCollaborationDemo" code-lang="vue"}
---
code: |
  <script setup lang="ts">
  import type { MarkdownEditorCollaboration } from '@talex-touch/tuffex/markdown-editor'
  import { ref } from 'vue'

  const content = ref(session.text())

  // session is the host's collaboration client (OT, CRDT, …); remote changes must be against the editor's current document
  const collaboration: MarkdownEditorCollaboration = {
    send: changes => session.send(changes),
    sendPresence: presence => session.sendPresence(presence),
    subscribe: ({ onChanges, onPeers }) => session.subscribe(onChanges, onPeers),
  }
  </script>

  <template>
    <TxMarkdownEditor
      v-model="content"
      :user="{ id: 'lin', name: 'Lin Xia', color: '#0ea5e9' }"
      :collaboration="collaboration"
    />
  </template>
---
::::

### Best Practices

- Keep `sanitize=true` for content written by users or providers.
- Use a controlled `mode` when the route or query stores it.
- In narrow editors such as comments or release notes, trim the toolbar with `toolbarActions` and turn off `slash` or `bubble` as needed.
- Have `uploadImage` and `ai` honour `signal`: it aborts when the user deletes the placeholder, stops or discards.
- If the host doesn't scan tuffex sources, add `MARKDOWN_EDITOR_ICON_CLASSES` from `src/toolbar-icons.ts` to the UnoCSS safelist.

## API Reference

### Props

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `modelValue` / `v-model` | `string` | `''` | The Markdown source. |
| `placeholder` | `string` | `''` | Placeholder in the editable modes. |
| `mode` | `'wysiwyg' \| 'source' \| 'preview'` | - | Controlled mode. |
| `defaultMode` | `'wysiwyg' \| 'source' \| 'preview'` | `'wysiwyg'` | Starting mode when uncontrolled. |
| `disabled` | `boolean` | `false` | Disables the toolbar, mode switcher, and editing surface. |
| `readonly` | `boolean` | `false` | Blocks editing; reading and mode switching still work. |
| `sanitize` | `boolean` | `true` | Sanitizes rendered HTML with DOMPurify; turn off only for trusted content. |
| `theme` | `'auto' \| 'light' \| 'dark'` | `'auto'` | Theme; `auto` follows the page. |
| `toolbar` | `boolean` | `true` | Shows the toolbar and mode switcher. |
| `toolbarActions` | `MarkdownEditorToolbarActionKey[]` | built-in set | Toolbar buttons, in order. |
| `minHeight` | `string \| number` | `220` | Minimum height of the editing area. |
| `maxHeight` | `string \| number` | - | Maximum height of the editing area. |
| `ariaLabel` | `string` | `'Markdown editor'` | Accessible name shared by both editing surfaces. |
| `linkPrompt` | `(selectedText: string) => string \| Promise<string>` | - | Replaces the built-in link field; return the URL, or `''` to cancel. |
| `math` | `boolean` | `true` | Renders `$…$` and `$$…$$` with KaTeX. |
| `emoji` | `boolean` | `true` | Renders `:shortcode:` and turns on `:` completion and the emoji picker. |
| `highlight` | `boolean` | `true` | `==text==` highlights and the highlighter's colours. |
| `callouts` | `boolean` | `true` | Shows quotes whose first line is `[!NOTE]`, `[!TIP]`, `[!IMPORTANT]`, `[!WARNING]` or `[!CAUTION]` as callouts. |
| `codeTheme` | `MarkdownEditorCodeTheme` | `'github'` | Syntax highlighting preset for code blocks with a language; `'none'` leaves them plain. |
| `slash` | `boolean` | `true` | In WYSIWYG, `/` at the start of a block opens the block menu. |
| `bubble` | `boolean` | `true` | In WYSIWYG, selecting text floats a formatting bar. |
| `ai` | `MarkdownEditorAi` | - | AI rewriting on the formatting bar; hidden without it. |
| `uploadImage` | `MarkdownEditorUploadImage` | - | Uploads pasted, dropped or chosen images and returns their hosted address; without it, the image button asks for an address. |
| `comments` / `v-model:comments` | `MarkdownEditorComment[]` | - | Comment threads; comments are hidden without it. |
| `user` | `MarkdownEditorUser` | `{ id: 'local', name: labels.you }` | The local user: the author of comments, and who collaborators see. |
| `collaboration` | `MarkdownEditorCollaboration` | - | Transport for real-time collaboration. |
| `statusBar` | `boolean` | `true` | Word count, character count and collaborators at the bottom. |
| `labels` | `Partial<MarkdownEditorLabels>` | English copy | Overrides the interface copy. |

### Events

| Event | Params | Description |
|------|--------|-------------|
| `update:modelValue` | `(value: string)` | Fires when the content changes. |
| `change` | `(value: string)` | Fires together with `update:modelValue`. |
| `update:mode` | `(mode: MarkdownEditorMode)` | Fires on a mode switch, for `v-model:mode`. |
| `mode-change` | `(mode: MarkdownEditorMode)` | Fires together with `update:mode`. |
| `focus` | `()` | Fires when the editing surface gains focus. |
| `blur` | `()` | Fires when the editing surface loses focus. |
| `update:comments` | `(comments: MarkdownEditorComment[])` | Fires when threads change or their ranges move with edits, for `v-model:comments`. |
| `comment-create` | `(comment: MarkdownEditorComment)` | Fires when a thread is created. |
| `comment-reply` | `(comment: MarkdownEditorComment, reply: MarkdownEditorCommentReply)` | Fires when a thread gets a reply. |
| `comment-resolve` | `(comment: MarkdownEditorComment)` | Fires when a thread is resolved or reopened; `resolved` tells which. |
| `comment-delete` | `(comment: MarkdownEditorComment)` | Fires when a thread is deleted. |
| `upload-error` | `(error: unknown, file: File)` | Fires when an image upload fails. |
| `ai-error` | `(error: unknown)` | Fires when an AI rewrite fails. |

### Exposed Methods

| Method | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `focus()` | Focuses the current mode's editing surface. |
| `blur()` | Blurs the current editing surface. |
| `setMode(mode)` | Switches the mode. |
| `getMode()` | Returns the current mode. |
| `getValue()` | Returns the current Markdown. |
| `setValue(value)` | Replaces the whole text as one edit: emits updates and sends it to collaborators. |
| `getSelection()` | Returns the selection as offsets into the Markdown source. |
| `setSelection(selection)` | Focuses and sets the selection. |
| `insert(markdown)` | Inserts Markdown at the selection, as a user edit. |

### Types

:::TuffCodeBlock{lang="ts"}
---
code: |
  type MarkdownEditorMode = 'wysiwyg' | 'source' | 'preview'

  type MarkdownEditorToolbarActionKey =
    | 'heading' | 'bold' | 'italic' | 'strike' | 'code' | 'highlight' | 'quote'
    | 'bulletList' | 'orderedList' | 'taskList' | 'link' | 'image' | 'table'
    | 'codeBlock' | 'math' | 'divider' | 'emoji' | 'undo' | 'redo'

  type MarkdownEditorCodeTheme = 'github' | 'one' | 'vitesse' | 'catppuccin' | 'solarized' | 'none'

  interface MarkdownEditorAiRequest {
    action: 'improve' | 'shorten' | 'expand' | 'fix' | 'translate' | 'custom'
    instruction: string // what the user typed, for custom
    text: string // the selected Markdown, which the answer replaces
    before: string // up to 2,000 characters of context on each side
    after: string
    signal: AbortSignal // aborts on stop, retry or discard
  }
  type MarkdownEditorAi = (request: MarkdownEditorAiRequest) => string | Promise<string> | AsyncIterable<string>

  type MarkdownEditorUploadImage = (
    file: File,
    context: { onProgress: (percent: number) => void, signal: AbortSignal },
  ) => Promise<string | { url: string, alt?: string, title?: string }>

  interface MarkdownEditorUser { id: string, name: string, color?: string, avatar?: string }

  interface MarkdownEditorComment {
    id: string
    from: number // a source range that moves with edits
    to: number
    quote: string // relocates the range when it no longer matches
    author: MarkdownEditorUser
    body: string
    createdAt: number
    resolved?: boolean
    replies?: MarkdownEditorCommentReply[]
  }

  // One replacement; every offset in a change set is against the document before it
  interface MarkdownTextChange { from: number, to: number, insert: string }

  interface MarkdownEditorCollaboration {
    send: (changes: MarkdownTextChange[]) => void
    sendPresence?: (presence: { selection: MarkdownEditorSelection | null, mode: MarkdownEditorMode }) => void
    subscribe: (handlers: {
      onChanges: (changes: MarkdownTextChange[]) => void // against the editor's current document
      onPeers?: (peers: MarkdownEditorPeer[]) => void
    }) => () => void
  }
---
:::

## Change Sets

Collaboration adapters merge concurrent edits with these functions, all exported from `@talex-touch/tuffex/markdown-editor`.

| Function | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `applyMarkdownChanges(doc, changes)` | Applies a change set to a text. |
| `composeMarkdownChanges(a, b, docLength)` | Combines two consecutive change sets into one. |
| `mapMarkdownPosition(pos, changes, assoc?)` | Where a position lands after a change set; `assoc` puts a position at an insertion before (`-1`) or after (`1`) the inserted text. |
| `transformMarkdownChanges(a, b, docLength)` | Rebases two concurrent change sets over each other and returns `[a', b']`; at the same insertion point, `a` goes first. |

## Overview

- Passing `mode` makes the mode controlled; otherwise `defaultMode` seeds it. All three modes share one Markdown document; preview takes no typing and disables the formatting buttons, but its task boxes still toggle.
- WYSIWYG renders block by block; when the caret enters bold, a link, inline math or another format, its Markdown marks appear and can be edited in place. `/` at the start of a block (`、` with a Chinese input method) opens the block menu.
- Selecting text floats a bar with formats, highlight colours, link, comment and AI. The AI's answer streams in and can show its changes word by word; replace, insert it below, try again or discard. `Esc` discards and restores the selection.
- An image goes in as a placeholder with progress, then becomes the address `uploadImage` returns; deleting the placeholder aborts the upload.
- Every edit commits as a change set, which moves the undo history, comment ranges and collaborators' carets. The local caret is sent at most every 50 ms; a collaborator's name shows for 2.5 s after their caret moves.
- Both editing modes share shortcuts: `Mod+B` bold, `Mod+I` italic, `Mod+E` inline code, `Mod+Shift+X` strikethrough, `Mod+Shift+H` highlight, `Mod+K` link, `Mod+Alt+1–6` headings (`Mod+Alt+0` back to a paragraph), `Mod+Alt+M` comment. The mode switcher is a `role="group"` of toggle buttons; `aria-pressed` marks the active mode.

## Technologies

- Source mode is CodeMirror 6; WYSIWYG is a contenteditable block view rendered from marked's tokens and mapped to the source character by character. Code blocks are coloured with the CSS Custom Highlight API; shiki, KaTeX and the AI panel load when first used.
- The built-in emoji data comes from emojilib 2.4.0 (MIT).
- Source: `packages/tuffex/packages/components/src/markdown-editor/`.

